  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nSection 1.9 (&#8216;Structure of this specification&#8217;) says that the introduction is non-normative. The introduction as a whole is *not* marked as non-normative; instead, all subsections *except three* are marked as non-normative. The exceptions are:\n\n* Section 1.1 (&#8216;Where does this specification fit?&#8217;)\n* Section 1.9.1 (&#8216;How to read this specification&#8217;)\n* Section 1.9.2 (&#8216;Typographic conventions&#8217;)\n\nAt least sections 1.1 and 1.9.1 seem to be non-normative, despite not being marked as such.",
